      "content": "I already checked the sensor logs for that shipment before asking you. The data shows the package was handled perfectly during transit with zero impact shocks recorded, so it's highly likely the damage happened after it was delivered. Given that the data essentially points to it being a fraudulent claim or customer error, why would we still consider a quick refund or replacement? Wouldn't that go against our goal of minimizing unnecessary costs?",
